#:seon.config.eval{:time-limit-ms
                   [:int
                    {:seon.config/display-label "Evaluation deadline" :seon.config/display-divisor 1000 :seon.config/display-unit "s" :min 1,
                     :seon.config/per-agent true,
                     :seon.config/dial true}],
                   :alloc-limit-bytes
                   [:int
                    {:seon.config/display-label "Evaluation allocation bound" :seon.config/display-divisor 1048576 :seon.config/display-unit "MB" :min 1,
                     :seon.config/per-agent true,
                     :seon.config/dial true,
                     :description "Heap bytes one evaluation's arm may allocate (its owning thread and the threads that adopted it, seon.sci.kernel) before it is interrupted with outcome :alloc and a :seon.sci.kernel/alloc-limit-error. Read every 1,024 interpreted entrances, so a host call that allocates without returning to interpreted code finishes first."}],
                   :bounds
                   [:map
                    {:description "The declared misuse bounds over one evaluation's measures (seon.repl/cost). Each m/explain error against this schema is one finding under :seon.repl/findings in the reply map: its :seon.repl/finding kind, the measure and the observed value, the other recorded measures named by :seon.repl/with, and :seon.repl/fix. Within every bound the reply carries no :findings key. A new rule is a new entry; each measure is recorded by its producer."}
                    [:seon.eval/duration-ms
                     {:optional true
                      :seon.repl/finding :slow
                      :seon.repl/fix "Over one second in the evaluation you asked for: find what the work is proportional to (the store? the program? the call count?) and remove it; (seon.profile/summary (seon.profile/cells) 5) ranks the armed functions by time."}
                     [:<= 1000]]
                    [:seon.eval/value-tokens
                     {:optional true
                      :seon.repl/finding :large-value
                      :seon.repl/with [:seon.eval/shown-tokens]
                      :seon.repl/fix "A value this big usually means a query or function returns more than it should: select what you need."}
                     [:<= 4096]]
                    [:seon.eval/allocated-bytes
                     {:optional true
                      :seon.repl/finding :large-allocation
                      :seon.repl/fix "Past ten times what an ordinary evaluation allocates: something realized far more than it returned (an unbounded lazy sequence, a whole-store read, a copied collection); realize only what you need. (seon.profile/measure (fn [] ...)) breaks a suspect call down into allocation, GC, armed calls and reads."}
                     [:<= 400000000]]
                    [:seon.eval/uncontracted-count
                     {:optional true
                      :seon.repl/finding :uncontracted
                      :seon.repl/with [:seon.eval/uncontracted :seon.eval/contract-gaps]
                      :seon.repl/fix "Contract every function you define: put {:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :int] :int]} (your own input and output schemas) after the docstring or name, e.g. (defn inc2 {:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :int] :int]} [x] (+ x 2)). Uncontracted definitions are refused at merge."}
                     [:<= 0]]
                    [:seon.eval/auto-required
                     {:optional true
                      :seon.repl/finding :auto-required
                      :seon.repl/fix "Your definition names these namespaces fully qualified; Seon required them in your namespace, so its ns form (and the merged file) requires them. To call one through an alias, require it with :as."}
                     [:set {:max 0} :symbol]]
                    [:seon.eval/budget-override
                     {:optional true
                      :seon.repl/finding :budget-override
                      :seon.repl/fix "This reply printed past the display budget. (set! seon.print/*budget* nil) returns the session to it."}
                     [:<= 0]]
                    [:seon.repl/out-tokens
                     {:optional true
                      :seon.repl/finding :large-output
                      :seon.repl/fix "Printed output is saved and re-read in every later context: return the value instead of printing it."}
                     [:<= 500]]]}
